                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "759b0f4a-6bdc-3c15-943c-c960e642705d",
                        "entry_id": "51f2d846-d32b-3c55-9cb4-d97c46529e21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Deeply rooted; persistent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca87e8eb-49b1-4a6a-baac-9d63cf88e817",
                                "sense_id": "759b0f4a-6bdc-3c15-943c-c960e642705d",
                                "text": "The first thing to bear in mind (especially if we ourselves belong to the clerico-academic-scientific type, the officially and conventionally “correct” type, “the deadly respectable” type, for which to ignore others is a besetting temptation) is that nothing can be more stupid than to bar out phenomena from our notice, merely because we are incapable of taking part in anything like them ourselves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fefcd081-5677-4751-bcaa-9350567f8239",
                                "sense_id": "759b0f4a-6bdc-3c15-943c-c960e642705d",
                                "text": "Rickie would not push himself. It was his besetting sin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b525a4b-4fef-4926-819e-1d2946813b13",
                                "sense_id": "759b0f4a-6bdc-3c15-943c-c960e642705d",
                                "text": "I did not then know the besetting sin of woman, the passion to discuss her private affairs with anyone who is willing to listen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d210f5e-c98e-3dfe-a31e-0ca3f2ddf4e6",
                        "entry_id": "51f2d846-d32b-3c55-9cb4-d97c46529e21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsessive"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47a0fb99-db0c-47f3-b03e-4a96ccdbe8d4",
                                "sense_id": "4d210f5e-c98e-3dfe-a31e-0ca3f2ddf4e6",
                                "text": "Neither were they connected with fear: he was conscious of no fear. Rather, they originated in a strange besetting desire to know what to do when the time came; a desire gigantically disproportionate to the few swift moments to which it referred; a wondering that was more like the wondering of some other spirit within his, than his own."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
